HELP 'TO_VECTOR';
name	description	example
VEC_FROMTEXT	Syntax:
VEC_FROMTEXT(text_string)

Converts a text representation of a vector to the internal binary
VECTOR format. The input should be a comma-separated list of numbers
enclosed in square brackets, e.g. '[1.0, 2.0, 3.0]'.

Aliases: TO_VECTOR(), STRING_TO_VECTOR().

	mysql> SELECT VEC_TOTEXT(VEC_FROMTEXT('[1, 2, 3]'));
        -> [1.000000,2.000000,3.000000]

HELP 'STRING_TO_VECTOR';
name	description	example
VEC_FROMTEXT	Syntax:
VEC_FROMTEXT(text_string)

Converts a text representation of a vector to the internal binary
VECTOR format. The input should be a comma-separated list of numbers
enclosed in square brackets, e.g. '[1.0, 2.0, 3.0]'.

Aliases: TO_VECTOR(), STRING_TO_VECTOR().

	mysql> SELECT VEC_TOTEXT(VEC_FROMTEXT('[1, 2, 3]'));
